# Giant letters: the oscillator can X1 runs at 2 MHz, though marked 4 MHz. Every count divides that clock, so each dot lasts twice as long and each line 128 µs: the TV free-runs, drawing the letters twice as wide, spilling off the screen.
machine typewriter
title "Giant letters"
brief "The letters on the TV are twice their size and spill off its edges, and the picture will not hold still."
fault clock X1 2MHz
